From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps print through ChromeOS's print preview

Flatpak apps print through xdg-desktop-portal's Print portal, which had no
backend: Print did nothing. xdg-desktop-portal-nickel's lets the app lay
out its pages (PDF) and asks Chrome:

- VmApplicationsService.NickelPrint(app name, title, h document) answers
  whether print preview opened. NickelPrint saves the PDF in
  /tmp/nickel-print (kept a day), opens it in a window of its own and
  ChromeOS's print preview over it, with its printers (Settings >
  Printers) and Save as PDF.

